# ALFa AI + monitoring usage — Rankings Bot

Rankings Bot is the **reference implementation**. Patterns here are copied by the
other bots, so keep them correct and drift-free. Full detail: [`AGENTS.md`](mdc:rankings-bot/AGENTS.md).

## ALFa AI (server-side only)

- The brain (LiteLLM proxy + orchestrator) runs on **`hub`**. This app calls LiteLLM
  through [`api/services/litellm_client.py`](mdc:rankings-bot/api/services/litellm_client.py).
- **Never** put LiteLLM/Ollama keys or base URLs in the frontend, and never call the
  LLM directly from client code. AI features go through a backend route that proxies LiteLLM.
- **Trust zones** (see [`docs/ALFA_AI_TRUST_ZONES_AND_ROLLOUT.md`](mdc:rankings-bot/docs/ALFA_AI_TRUST_ZONES_AND_ROLLOUT.md)):
  - `public_web` → `POST /api/ai-narrative/demo-ask`, alias `public-chat`, demo bundle only.
  - `app_authenticated` → `POST /api/ai-narrative/ask`, alias `app-chat` (or `LITELLM_MODEL_PAGE_QUESTION`), JWT required.
  - `internal` → ALFa AI orchestrator `/api/runs`; never mix internal data into public prompts/logs.
- **Model aliases are a contract** owned by `alfa-ai/deploy/litellm_config.yaml`. Do not
  invent new alias names in this repo; request them in `alfa-ai` first.
- **Telemetry:** every LLM call logs to `ollama_activity_log`. New call sites must pass
  `feature`, `trust_zone` metadata, and populate `duration_seconds` + token counts.

## Sanctioned exception — xAI Grok vision

[`api/services/grok_client.py`](mdc:rankings-bot/api/services/grok_client.py) calls xAI
**Grok** (`grok-4` vision) directly for pool coaching. This is an **intentional** product
path, not a workaround — the LiteLLM/Ollama/Petals swarm does not serve vision coaching.
Do **not** reroute it through LiteLLM without a vision alias on the brain + product sign-off.
Key stays server-side env only.

## Monitoring (central stack on `apps`)

- Production uses the central `monitoring` repo stack — **no** per-bot Prometheus/Grafana
  in production. Details: [`docs/MONITORING_RANKINGS_BOT.md`](mdc:rankings-bot/docs/MONITORING_RANKINGS_BOT.md).
- API exposes `/metrics` on `8003`. `http_requests_total{status}` uses a **status class**
  label (`2xx`…`5xx`) — match it **exactly** (`status="5xx"`), never rely on loose regex.
- Scrape job `rankings-bot-api`; alerts in `monitoring/prometheus/rules/rankings_alerts.yml`;
  dashboards in `monitoring/grafana/dashboards/rankings_bot_*.json`.

## Drift check (mandatory after changes)

After any AI/monitoring change, verify: client matches `litellm_config.yaml` aliases,
telemetry fields populated, alert/dashboard label selectors match emitted labels, and
docs (`AGENTS.md`, the two docs above) still match the code. See
[`engineering-standards-and-drift-control`](mdc:.cursor/rules/engineering-standards-and-drift-control.mdc).
